fact WorkItem(id: "WI-106", description: some(value: "Auto-generate <Sort>.cases / <Sort>.induction rules from sort/enum constructor structure during load. Generation rules (proposal 025 lines 205-209): for each entity constructor emit one case; fields of the entity's own sort type contribute induction hypotheses (`?P(?field)` premise under a forall binding the field); non-recursive fields are universally quantified; entities with no recursive fields are base cases. Examples in 025: Color.cases (finite enum), List.induction (single-recursion), Tree.induction (multi-recursion with two IHs). Implementation: kb/load.rs post-pass that walks each user-defined sort, synthesizes the induction Rule, registers it in the sort's scope under the qualified name `<sort_qname>.induction` (or `.cases` for non-recursive enums). Acceptance: loading a file with `enum List { entity nil entity cons(head: T, tail: List[T]) end }` produces a queryable rule List.induction whose body matches proposal 025 line 170-173. Prerequisite for WI-101 (consumer tactic)."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-104", "WI-105"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-04-27T10:56:39Z"))

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-106", author: "claude", content: "Recursive-position IH form added. emit_induction_rule classifies fields via field_is_recursive (Simple TypeExpr with remapped symbol equal to sort). Entities with recursive fields emit forall_impl(binders, IHs, [consequent]). Non-recursive ctors keep flat ho_apply. Test recursive_field_emits_inductive_hypothesis verifies for enum IntList. Printed form matches proposal 025. All 605 anthill-core tests pass. Parameterised sorts still skip emission upstream; covered by WI-107.", at: "2026-04-27T10:56:45Z")
